    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Vinnie Pasquantino** anchoring the utility spot as our highest-rated asset at 70.66. His projection is bolstered by a significant 14% platoon edge against Burnes, combined with favorable wind conditions that lift his floor. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (66.30) and **Gabriel Moreno** (64.50) are elite starts; both benefit from advantageous matchups against mid-rotation arms and high-order placement. **James Wood** remains a must-start at 63.47, as his elite xwOBA metrics and leadoff positioning against Mize provide the best opportunity to capitalize on base-path activity, a crucial factor as we continue to hunt stolen bases to remain competitive in our tightest category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Austin Riley** on the bench. Despite a respectable 57.59 score, he fell just short of the efficiency thresholds maintained by **Josh Naylor** and **Travis Bazzana**. While **Austin Riley** offers power upside, the optimizer favored the lineup spots and platoon advantages assigned to **Travis Bazzana** and **Brice Turang** in their respective matchups. We remain wary of **Seiya Suzuki** and **Mickey Moniak**, both of whom are facing dangerous arms in Misiorowski and Schlittler, respectively; while their scores justify a start, the sub-3.00 xERA of their opponents introduces a non-trivial risk of an early exit for our hitters. We continue to monitor the status of **Corbin Carroll** and **Jose Caballero**, who remain sidelined, as we rely on the depth provided by **Zach McKinstry** to fill the final outfield slot despite his lower-order placement.",
